ults from a corresponding theoretical model. Recorded data include force-versus-displacement curves for springs used, switching thresholds for the built hysterons, and time evolution of a coupled hysteron system.\n2. \"Kinematic-model.nb\": Mathematica notebook for calculating the switching thresholds for two coupled rotor hysterons using the exact kinematic model.\n3. \"t-graph-maker.ipynb\": Jupyter notebook for determining stable states and transition pathways in a system of N coupled hysterons.", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 110183, "created_date": "2026-04-14T07:01:43Z", "modified_date": "2026-04-14T07:01:46Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["Soft matter physics", "mechanical metamaterials", "hysteresis effects", "mechanical memory", "Mechanical Computing"], "keywords": ["Soft matter physics", "mechanical metamaterials", "hysteresis effects", "mechanical memory", "Mechanical Computing"], "categories": [{"id": 896, "title": "Thermodynamics and Statistical Physics", "parent_id": 6, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}], "references": ["https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-70913-2"], "has_linked_file": false, "citation": "Paulsen, Joseph (2026). Dataset and code for rotor-based mechanical hysteron experiments and theory. figshare. Dataset. https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.28856705.v1", "related_materials": [{"id": 275481426, "identifier": "10.1038/s41467-026-70913-2", "title": "Mechanical hysterons with tunable interactions of general sign", "relation": "IsSupplementTo", "identifier_type": "DOI", "is_linkout": true, "link": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-70913-2"}], "is_embargoed": false, "embargo_date": null, "embargo_type": null, "embargo_title": "", "embargo_reason": "", "embargo_options": [], "i